# Go architecture

```
cmd/permitdenied/main.go   # window title, RunGame only (~25 lines)
internal/game/             # scene, Update, input, sim, combat, beat, const.go
internal/dozer lot run threats fx audio render
assets/embed.go            # go:embed usable/*
```

No `pkg/`. No interfaces-for-one-implementation. Unexported fields unless a test in another package needs them. No goroutines — the sim is single-threaded in `Update`. Geometry is Go literals in `lot/lot.go`, not JSON level files.

## Loop

`Update` is logic. `Draw` is render. Never mutate sim state in `Draw`. `dt` is `1.0/60.0` every Update; do not use a Draw-frame delta.

Read keyboard/touch **once** in `game.readInput()` into `Input{Throttle, Steer, BladeToggle}`. `dozer` and `threats` never call `IsKeyPressed`.

Every new tunable goes in `internal/game/const.go` with a comment pointing at the spec line. Do not sprinkle magic numbers.

## Ebitengine

Use `ColorScale`, not deprecated `ColorM`. Use `ebiten.AppendTouchIDs`, not `TouchIDs()`. Gameplay sprites: `ebiten.FilterNearest`.

## Verify

```
go test ./...
go run ./cmd/permitdenied
```

Keep green: `TestForwardVector`, `TestMultTable`, `TestSpawnWOneSecond`, `TestSpawnAHalfSecond`, `TestBladeDownDropsSheriffHP`, plus beat/combat/atlas tests already in tree. Local Windows package: `build.bat` → `dist\permitdenied.exe` (do not commit the exe).
